        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Robot vacuums handle pet hair well, and on <strong class="text-white">hard floors and low-pile carpet they handle it very well indeed</strong> — because they run daily and hair never gets a chance to accumulate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose on <strong class="text-white">dual rubber rollers, a bagged self-emptying dock and good obstacle avoidance</strong>, not on Pascal figures. Then keep the two-minute weekly habit of cutting hair off the brushes — that single task is what separates a machine that still cleans well in year three from one that quietly stopped in month three.
          </p>
